---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import AltitudePlanningInteractions from '../components/AltitudePlanningInteractions.astro';
import {altitudeReviewedAt,altitudeSources,altitudePoints,altitudeJourneys,altitudeFilterOptions,altitudePointFor,altitudeDifference,buildAltitudePlan,altitudeFaqs} from '../data/altitudePlanning';
const initial=buildAltitudePlan();
const number=(value:number)=>value.toLocaleString('en-CA');
const faqSchema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:altitudeFaqs.map(faq=>({'@type':'Question',name:faq.question,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:faq.answer}}))};
---
<BaseLayout title="Banff Elevation Guide: Compare Mountain Visits & Overnight Plans" description="Compare sourced elevations for Banff, Lake Louise, Moraine Lake and resort terminals. Plan the actual journey, overnight stay and medical questions without a personal risk score." lastUpdated={altitudeReviewedAt}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')} />
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Elevation Guide'}]} /></div>
  <section class="altitude-hero"><div class="container"><span class="badge">Know the place, plan the journey</span><h1>Elevation in Banff &amp; Lake Louise</h1><p>A town stay, a lakeshore visit and a ski-area summit are different plans. Compare the named points, arrange the way down and separate the day’s highest stop from where you sleep.</p><a class="btn btn-accent" href="#elevation-planner">Compare five journeys ↓</a><p class="review">Sources reviewed <time datetime={altitudeReviewedAt}>October 29, 2026</time>. No personal health information is requested.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section altitude-intro"><div class="container">
    <h2>Elevation is one part of the plan</h2>
    <p>Banff’s published townsite reference is <strong>1,383 m</strong>. That does not describe every mountain destination around it. Lake Louise community, its lakeshore and the ski resort are separate places, and riding a lift changes elevation without showing whether a person is ready for the visit.</p>
    <p>The <a href={altitudeSources.cdc.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CDC Yellow Book</a> identifies unacclimatized travellers sleeping at <strong>2,450 m or higher, sometimes lower</strong>, as at risk of altitude illness. It also explains that a day visit followed by a lower overnight is less stressful than sleeping high. These are general principles, not a safe/unsafe boundary for an individual. There is no simple screening test, and fitness does not protect against altitude illness.</p>
    <p>Use this page to prepare an itinerary and questions. A clinician familiar with altitude medicine can discuss your actual trip and health circumstances privately; this tool does not diagnose symptoms, prescribe medication or clear anyone to travel.</p>
    <nav class="altitude-jumps" aria-label="Elevation guide sections"><a href="#elevation-points">Published points</a><a href="#elevation-planner">Journey comparison</a><a href="#altitude-preparation">Preparation</a><a href="#altitude-help">If someone is unwell</a><a href="#altitude-faq">Questions &amp; sources</a></nav>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section altitude-points" id="elevation-points" aria-labelledby="elevation-points-title"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-header"><span class="badge">Compare like with like</span><h2 id="elevation-points-title">Nine published reference points</h2><p>Metres above sea level, as named by each publisher. Different points and rounded operator descriptions can differ; these are not surveyed hotel-room, trailhead or entrance measurements.</p></div>
    <div class="altitude-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Published elevation reference points"><table><caption>Point identity and source matter as much as the number</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Published point</th><th scope="col">Elevation</th><th scope="col">What the number describes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{altitudePoints.map(point=><tr data-altitude-point={point.id}><th scope="row">{point.label}</th><td>{number(point.metres)} m</td><td>{point.note} <a href={altitudeSources[point.source].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{altitudeSources[point.source].label} ↗</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="altitude-small">Lake Louise community is <strong>1,536 m</strong>; <strong>1,731 m</strong> belongs to the lakeshore in Parks Canada’s 2025 map. Resort top, terminal and overnight accommodation elevations should not be substituted for one another.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section altitude-planner" id="elevation-planner" aria-labelledby="elevation-planner-title"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-header"><span class="badge">Build the whole outing</span><h2 id="elevation-planner-title">Compare the journey and the overnight</h2><p>Select a journey to focus the cards, then decide what needs checking about your stay. All comparisons and source links remain readable without JavaScript.</p></div>
    <form id="altitude-form" hidden><div><label for="altitude-journey">Which journey are you considering?</label><select id="altitude-journey" name="altitude_journey">{altitudeFilterOptions.journey.map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></div><div><label for="altitude-overnight">What happens after the outing?</label><select id="altitude-overnight" name="altitude_overnight">{altitudeFilterOptions.overnight.map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></div><div class="altitude-actions"><button class="btn" type="submit">Update comparison</button><button class="btn btn-outline" type="reset">Show all / reset</button><button class="btn btn-outline" id="altitude-copy" type="button">Copy public settings link</button></div></form>
    <p id="altitude-url-note" role="status" hidden></p><p id="altitude-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">{initial.summary}</p>
    <aside class="altitude-overnight"><h3>Make the overnight explicit</h3><p id="altitude-overnight-question">{initial.overnightQuestion}</p><p>Changing this choice changes questions, not a health conclusion. The tool does not assume that you sleep at the high point or that returning lower prevents illness.</p></aside>
    <p class="altitude-comparison-note"><strong>Point difference is not hiking gain.</strong> Each card subtracts its two named elevations. It does not calculate total ascent, distance, time, exertion, oxygen level, travel feasibility or a safe route.</p>
    <div class="altitude-grid">{altitudeJourneys.map(journey=>{const from=altitudePointFor(journey.from),to=altitudePointFor(journey.to);return <article class="altitude-card" data-altitude-journey={journey.id} aria-labelledby={`altitude-name-${journey.id}`}><h3 id={`altitude-name-${journey.id}`}>{journey.name}</h3><dl><div><dt>From</dt><dd>{from.label}: {number(from.metres)} m</dd></div><div><dt>To</dt><dd>{to.label}: {number(to.metres)} m</dd></div><div><dt>Difference between these points</dt><dd>+{number(altitudeDifference(journey))} m — not total ascent</dd></div></dl><p>{journey.context}</p><h4>Join the arrangements</h4><p>{journey.question}</p><p class="altitude-small">{journey.scope}</p><p><a href={journey.href}>{journey.linkLabel} →</a></p><a class="altitude-small" href={altitudeSources[journey.source].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{altitudeSources[journey.source].label} ↗</a></article>;})}</div>
    <div class="altitude-copy-area"><p id="altitude-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="altitude-copy-fallback" hidden><label for="altitude-copy-text">Public settings link — select and copy</label><textarea id="altitude-copy-text" rows="3" readonly></textarea></div><p class="altitude-small">The copied link contains only the two public choices. It excludes other address-bar parameters and sends nothing to a provider.</p></div>
    <noscript><p>The full five-card comparison is above. Record your actual overnight address and return arrangements separately; no online screening is needed to read this guide.</p></noscript>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section" id="altitude-preparation" aria-labelledby="altitude-preparation-title"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-header"><span class="badge">Before committing</span><h2 id="altitude-preparation-title">Five useful planning questions</h2></div>
    <ol class="altitude-steps"><li><strong>What is the real activity?</strong> A sightseeing terminal, a lesson area and an alpine hike have different physical, weather and access requirements. Check the actual route or product, rather than its highest advertised number.</li><li><strong>Where will you sleep?</strong> Write down the night before and after a higher outing. Ask the accommodation about its actual location and access; no fixed Day 2 or Day 3 rule establishes acclimatization.</li><li><strong>Can you shorten the day?</strong> Keep an arrival-day option close to your stay and protect the return transport. Use <a href="/towns/">base comparisons</a>, <a href="/winter-stays/">winter stays</a> and the <a href="/what-to-do-today/">outing chooser</a> to build alternatives.</li><li><strong>What needs a private medical discussion?</strong> Bring the real elevations, ascent pattern and remoteness to a clinician if you have health concerns, a previous altitude illness or a rapid high-altitude itinerary. Do not change prescribed treatment using a travel webpage.</li><li><strong>What is the current access?</strong> Read <a href="/conditions/">road and trail source handoffs</a> and <a href="/weather/">weather planning</a>. An elevation table does not establish open terrain, clear trails or winter suitability. Check the <a href="/trails/">specific trail</a> or <a href="/ski-day-planner/">resort day</a> separately.</li></ol>
    <p>The <a href={altitudeSources.nhs.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NHS prevention guidance</a> supports a gradual approach, avoiding dehydration and avoiding alcohol while travelling or climbing higher. A fixed water quota or “aggressive hydration” is not an altitude-clearance method. This page supplies no medication or dosing instructions.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section altitude-help" id="altitude-help" aria-labelledby="altitude-help-title"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-header"><span class="badge">Respond to illness, not a score</span><h2 id="altitude-help-title">If someone feels unwell higher up</h2></div>
    <div class="altitude-help-grid"><article><h3>Stop going higher and speak up</h3><p><a href={altitudeSources.alberta.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MyHealth Alberta</a> lists headache, appetite loss, nausea, dizziness, weakness and disturbed sleep among possible altitude-illness symptoms. These symptoms can overlap other illnesses. Do not dismiss them as a normal first night or use this list to diagnose the cause.</p><p>Tell companions, rest and do not continue higher while symptoms remain. Worsening symptoms or moderate-to-severe illness require descent and medical help. Do not leave an ill person to descend alone. Ask for professional advice rather than waiting for a promised recovery time.</p><p>For non-emergency health advice in Alberta, <a href="tel:811">call Health Link 811</a>. It is <a href={altitudeSources.healthLink.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">a health-advice and care-navigation service</a>, not mountain rescue.</p></article><article class="altitude-emergency"><h3>Emergency signs: get help immediately</h3><p>Confusion, difficulty walking straight or coordinating movements, breathlessness at rest, blue or grey lips, or being difficult to wake require urgent medical help. The <a href={altitudeSources.nhs.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NHS urgent-warning list</a> treats these as serious signs. They are not a “moderate” category to monitor while continuing.</p><p><strong>Call <a href="tel:911">911</a> for an emergency.</strong> In a mountain emergency, name Banff National Park, give the exact location and request Parks Canada mountain rescue. Seek descent with assistance when possible; follow emergency instructions and do not send the person down alone.</p><p><a href={altitudeSources.rescue.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Parks Canada’s rescue page</a> gives <a href="tel:+14037624506">+1 403 762 4506</a> for a satellite phone. Cell coverage is unreliable in mountain areas. Plan and learn your emergency communication method before leaving; rescue access and timing are not guaranteed.</p></article></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section altitude-faq" id="altitude-faq" aria-labelledby="altitude-faq-title"><div class="container"><div class="section-header"><span class="badge">Clear distinctions</span><h2 id="altitude-faq-title">Elevation questions</h2></div>{altitudeFaqs.map(faq=><details><summary>{faq.question}</summary><p>{faq.answer}</p></details>)}</div></section>
  <section class="section altitude-source-section" aria-labelledby="altitude-sources-title"><div class="container"><h2 id="altitude-sources-title">Sources and what was checked</h2><p>Reviewed <time datetime={altitudeReviewedAt}>October 29, 2026</time>. Health guidance comes from the identified public-health publishers; elevation points come from the named town, Parks Canada map and operators. Source editions and access scopes matter. This page has no live medical, weather, trail or operator feed.</p><ul>{Object.values(altitudeSources).map(source=><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.label} ↗</a><p>{source.scope}</p></li>)}</ul></div></section>
  <AltitudePlanningInteractions />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .altitude-hero{padding:4rem 0;background:var(--color-primary);color:white}.altitude-hero h1{color:white;font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.2rem);max-width:19ch;line-height:1.1;margin:.8rem 0 1.4rem}.altitude-hero p{max-width:48rem;line-height:1.8;color:#f2eee4}.altitude-hero .review{font-size:.84rem;margin:1.5rem 0 0}.altitude-intro p,.altitude-steps li,.altitude-help p,.altitude-source-section p{line-height:1.8;max-width:66rem}.altitude-jumps{display:flex;gap:.8rem 1.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.5rem}.altitude-points,.altitude-help,.altitude-source-section{background:var(--color-bg-alt)}.altitude-table{overflow:auto;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px;background:white}.altitude-table table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:40rem;text-align:left}.altitude-table caption{text-align:left;padding:1rem;font-weight:700}.altitude-table th,.altitude-table td{padding:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);vertical-align:top;line-height:1.6}.altitude-table td:nth-child(2){white-space:nowrap;font-weight:700}.altitude-small{font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-light)}.altitude-planner,#elevation-points,#altitude-help,#altitude-faq{scroll-margin-top:7rem}.altitude-planner [hidden]{display:none!important}#altitude-form{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;padding:1.4rem;border:1px solid var(--color-border);background:var(--color-bg-alt);border-radius:8px}.altitude-planner label{display:block;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.5rem}.altitude-planner select,.altitude-planner textarea{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;min-height:48px;padding:.75rem;border:1px solid #a9b5a6;border-radius:5px;background:white;font:inherit;color:var(--color-text)}.altitude-actions{grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.altitude-actions button{min-height:48px;white-space:normal}#altitude-status{font-weight:700;margin:1.4rem 0}.altitude-overnight{border-left:4px solid var(--color-accent);padding:1.2rem 1.5rem;background:#f4f0e6;margin:1.5rem 0}.altitude-overnight h3{margin:0 0 .7rem}.altitude-overnight p{line-height:1.8;margin:.5rem 0}.altitude-comparison-note{line-height:1.8}.altitude-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.altitude-card{border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-top:4px solid var(--color-primary);border-radius:8px;padding:1.4rem;min-width:0}.altitude-card h3{font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 1rem}.altitude-card h4{margin:1.2rem 0 .5rem}.altitude-card p{line-height:1.8}.altitude-card dl{margin:1rem 0}.altitude-card dl>div{padding:.6rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)}.altitude-card dt{font-size:.78rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700}.altitude-card dd{margin:.3rem 0 0;line-height:1.6}.altitude-card a,.altitude-source-section a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.altitude-copy-area{margin-top:1.5rem}.altitude-copy-area [role=status]{font-weight:700}.altitude-steps{padding-left:1.4rem}.altitude-steps li{padding-left:.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.altitude-help-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.5rem}.altitude-help-grid article{background:white;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px;min-width:0}.altitude-help-grid .altitude-emergency{border-left:5px solid #9c3e31}.altitude-faq details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border);padding:1.2rem 0}.altitude-faq summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;min-height:44px}.altitude-faq details p{line-height:1.8;max-width:65rem}.altitude-source-section li{margin-bottom:1.2rem}.altitude-source-section li p{font-size:.85rem;margin:.4rem 0}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,textarea:focus-visible,.altitude-table:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ad792b;outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:720px){#altitude-form,.altitude-grid,.altitude-help-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.altitude-actions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr}.altitude-hero{padding:3rem 0}.altitude-card,.altitude-help-grid article{padding:1.15rem}.altitude-overnight{padding:1rem}.altitude-jumps a{min-height:38px}}
</style>
